{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/3568-gold-dollar-in-the-demo-spoilers","id":3568,"title":"Gold dollar in the demo *spoilers*","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-05T09:34:00-08:00","id":3568,"title":"Gold dollar in the demo *spoilers*","content":"I'm a little confused by the demo and wondered if some of the American posters can help me. In the demo, the angel Quorum uses a gold dollar as a tracking device, and it's stated that it's not been properly disguised. Now my confusion comes because I thought dollar coins were largely collectors items and not things you'd use as normal money, and certainly not something you'd give to a busker. However the demo doesn't seem to indicate that this is in itself odd behavior.<br /> <br /> Can anyone help clear this up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T10:03:04-08:00","id":3583,"title":"","content":"That is easy to clear up - you are incorrect in your previous understating. Dollar coins are standard circulated currency, they are just not used as often as bills by most people. They have been gold color since the <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sacagawea </span></span></span>coin minted in 2000, and continues to be gold-ish looking with the new former presidents theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>J. T. Legal</b><br /> The other kind of rules lawyer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/334-technocratjt","name":"TechnocratJT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar334_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T10:23:53-08:00","id":3596,"title":"","content":"Yeah they aren't used often but they are common enough. The problem is most people don't like to carry around change especially not coins.<br /> <br /> Most vending machines will give me dollar coins for change instead of paper because it's easier for them to handle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T10:50:55-08:00","id":3612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/3568-gold-dollar-in-the-demo-spoilers#post3568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little confused by the demo and wondered if some of the American posters can help me. In the demo, the angel Quorum uses a gold dollar as a tracking device, and it's stated that it's not been properly disguised. Now my confusion comes because I thought dollar coins were largely collectors items and not things you'd use as normal money, and certainly not something you'd give to a busker. However the demo doesn't seem to indicate that this is in itself odd behavior.<br /> <br /> Can anyone help clear this up?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to think it's a Canadian Dollar (not unheard of in Seattle, I'd think), and that's what they mean by it not being properly disguised.<br /> <br /> As far as I know, dollar coins <i>are </i>sometimes used as currency, but it's uncommon enough that you'd think twice about being given one. The federal government has tried to popularise them at various times, but that effort's largely failed. According to Wikipedia, more recent coins are collectables, but before 2012 there's a bit of a surplus.<br /> <br /> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Presidential_$1_Coin_Program<br /> <br /> Edit: I'll add that I'm not an American, so I might be talking complete nonsense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T12:43:54-08:00","id":3694,"title":"","content":"Thanks all for the quick responses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd like to think it's a Canadian Dollar (not unheard of in Seattle, I'd think), and that's what they mean by it not being properly disguised. </div> </div> </div>It's the angelic script written on the coin. Unless Canada is actually the God-Machine..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T00:24:19-08:00","id":4128,"title":"","content":"Naw, I get dollar coins as change for lightrail tickets all the time. People tend to give you a look like &quot;seriously?&quot; When you pay for stuff with them, but they're perfectly usable and wouldn't be cause for suspicion on their own. It's pretty much like paying for anything in change, people would just rather handle paper than coins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T07:19:27-08:00","id":4288,"title":"","content":"A lot of times when I go to cons (Origins, GenCon, etc.) I'll get a roll of dollar coins to use in tips jars and for coffee and so on. Also, they're a good size to flip between my knuckles, and they're bigger than quarters, which made a dollar coin a good fit for what I wanted in the demo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:17:25-08:00","id":4394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/3568-gold-dollar-in-the-demo-spoilers?p=3694#post3694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the angelic script written on the coin. Unless Canada is actually the God-Machine..</div> </div> </div> </div>I was being facetious. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ...and yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T00:57:46-08:00","id":6678,"title":"","content":"They're more common than a $2 bill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><b